From b17b8b71219cc9e182e78213361b8e974051ba81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: phantom-ref re-resolution borrows kept
 replica readers and reuses hub task-key scans

Card E P1 (t_01a1d59e5543daa1): on hermes-hub one displayed card with an active
suspected_hallucinated_references event made every GET /board open 21 SQLite
connections (each Board replica twice plus hub.db) and scan ~20k hub replica
task keys for its short-form ref: ~79 ms of a ~130 ms GET (live in-process
profile, 30 GETs at the Desktop's 3.9 s cadence).

- Board replica lookups (replica_tasks/replica_prefixes) and the hub lookup
  (replica_task_resolution) use kanban_session_activity.cached_ro, with one retry
  when the kept reader is evicted while waiting. An idle autocommit reader holds
  no snapshot, so every lookup still sees the latest commit.
- hub_tasks_found reuses answers while the hub replica's task-row probe
  (count, count(seq), max(seq), total(seq)) and file identity are unchanged;
  after a pull a known-absent ref is re-checked only against rows above the old
  max(seq) (hermes-hub stamps every replica write with its monotonic feed seq,
  the invariant kanban_replica_rows and _remote_read_memo already rely on); a
  known-present ref, a lower max(seq), rows without seq, or a replaced file
  look up in full. Freshness (offline/last_ok) is still read and judged per call.

Live hub A/B, same process environment, 25 GETs at 3.9 s with cProfile:
median 131 ms -> 49 ms per board GET (diagnostics projection 110 -> 30 ms).
Tests: 3 perf tests RED on the original source with 10 exactness controls
GREEN, all 13 GREEN after; 67 related tests pass.
